title: Discontent in the Commonwealth Army
subtitle:  The <span style="color: #808080;">reactionary</span> nest begins to voice its discontent aloud.
view-if: army_loyalty <= 0 and marcher_in_government and not rubicon and army_minister_party != "Marcher"
on-arrival: army_angry = 1
tags: event
new-page: true
max-visits: 1
face-image: img/portraits/SchleicherKurt.jpg

= Discontent in the Commonwealth Army

The Commonwealth Army, despite its evident bias toward right-wing <span style="color: #808080;">reactionary</span> politics, has long portrayed itself as a non-partisan, neutral force in Commonwealth affairs. Throughout most of the Unity Republic’s history, it has largely refrained from overt political interference. However, Defense Minister Ravabelle—alongside his longtime ally Kurt von Staal and Chief of the Army Kurt von Hammerton-Equord—has now made public the military’s growing disagreements and concerns with the <span style="color: #c00000;">**Marchers**</span>.

The Commonwealth Army remains widely respected across the political spectrum—except among the left-wing parties. Staal, long known as a political schemer, may attempt to exploit this to undermine our standing among our allies. We can either offer concessions to placate the military, or hold firm and do nothing at all.

- @concessions
- @idc
- @reform

@concessions
title: Perhaps another battleship will keep them happy?
subtitle: Conceding to the Commonwealth Army is viewed as a betrayal of our core values.
choose-if: reformist_strength >= labor_strength and reformist_strength >= left_strength and budget >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: [? if (labor_strength > reformist_strength) or (left_strength > reformist_strength): Our party refuses to tolerate concessions to the Commonwealth Army. ?][? if budget < 1: We lack the necessary budget. ?]
on-arrival: army_loyalty += 0.2; army_militancy += 1; left_dissent += 30; labor_dissent += 25; center_dissent += 20; reformist_dissent += 10; budget -= 1; commons_marcher -= 6; disfavored_marcher -= 6; burgher_marcher -= 2; faithful_marcher -= 2; guild_marcher += 2; nationalism += 8; pacifism -= 3; gold_left += 1; ddp_right += 1; ddp_cohesion -= 1; dufour_angry -= 25

We have accepted Staal’s demands for increased funding toward the army’s modernization program, securing the purchase of new equipment for the small force. This decision has drawn intense criticism from the <span style="color: #700000;">**Communists**</span> and many within our own party, who condemn the diversion of funds into the black hole of the defense budget instead of toward welfare for women and children.

@reform
title: Fire these rabble rousers immediately!
subtitle: The bourgeois parties will not be pleased.
choose-if: (coalition_dissent <= 0 and (unionist_relation >= 60 or (not in_grand_coalition and not in_weimar_coalition))) or in_left_front
unavailable-subtitle: We lack the leverage—or sympathy—among our coalition partners.
on-arrival: coalition_dissent += 1 if in_weimar_coalition or in_grand_coalition; burgher_marcher -= 2; guild_marcher -= 2; landed_marcher -= 2; unionist_relation -= 5; ddp_relation -= 5 if ddp_ideology != "Left"; gold_relation -= 8; lvp_relation -= 5; lvp_right += 2; gold_right += 2; ddp_right += 1; ddp_cohesion -= 1; dufour_angry += 25; army_minister = "Oster"; groener_explode = 1; army_loyalty += 0.2; coup_progress += 3; capital_strike_progress += 1
face-image: img/portraits/oster.jpg

Our request to dismiss Roland Ravabelle has been approved by our coalition partners. He is replaced by Hans Oster, a relatively minor officer in the Commonwealth Army. While Oster shares the nationalist leanings common within the military and is conservative enough to be accepted as Ravabelle’s successor, our lack of control over the Commonwealth Army Ministry limits us—we can only remove a handful of officials involved in political interference.

Staal has been dismissed from the Office for Ministerial Affairs, and von Hammerton, for now, has remained notably quiet.

@idc
title: What are they going to do? Coup us?
on-arrival: coalition_dissent += 2 if in_weimar_coalition or in_grand_coalition; commons_marcher -= 2 if pacifism < 5; burgher_marcher -= 2; burgher_marcher -= 2 if pacifism < 5; guild_marcher -= 4; guild_marcher -= 2 if pacifism < 5; landed_marcher -= 4; landed_marcher -= 2 if pacifism < 5; unionist_relation -= 10; ddp_relation -= 10 if ddp_ideology != "Left"; gold_relation -= 15; lvp_relation -= 15; lvp_right += 6; gold_right += 6; ddp_right += 2; ddp_cohesion -= 2; dufour_angry += 100; coup_progress += 5; capital_strike_progress += 3

The Commonwealth Army won’t go so far as to overthrow us, but Staal’s decade-long web of connections is proving effective. We are also the victim of a renewed propaganda campaign by the nationalist parties[? if pacifism >= 5:, which has fortunately failed to gain traction?]. [? if president == "DuFour": As a key figure in President DuFour’s camarilla, he has played a major role in stoking the old man’s growing hostility toward us. ?]
